package pages

templ Page() {
	<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-4xl px-6 py-14">
		<h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Starter guide</h1>
		<p class="mt-2 text-slate-600">
			This starter keeps things simple: Templ for UI, HTMX for navigation, and small JS islands for state.
		</p>

		<section class="mt-10 space-y-4">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Edit the UI</h2>
			<ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
				<li><code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5">views/pages/index.templ</code> updates the homepage.</li>
				<li><code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5">views/layouts/base.templ</code> controls the global shell.</li>
				<li>Reusable bits live in <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5">views/components</code>.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-10 space-y-4">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Add a new page</h2>
			<ol class="space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
				<li>1. Create <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5">views/pages/your-page/index.templ</code>.</li>
				<li>2. Run <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5">make gen</code> to update routes.</li>
				<li>3. Visit <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5">/your-page</code> in the browser.</li>
			</ol>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-10 space-y-4">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Add business logic</h2>
			<ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
				<li>Create handlers in <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5">handlers/</code> to handle API work.</li>
				<li>Register custom routes in <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5">internal/routes/register.go</code> inside <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5">RegisterCustom</code>.</li>
				<li>Use HTMX to fetch partials by returning only the page component.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-10 space-y-4">
			<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Local state islands</h2>
			<ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
				<li>Create a module in <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5">views/scripts/modules</code>.</li>
				<li>Add <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5">data-module="your-module"</code> to markup.</li>
				<li>Run <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1 py-0.5">npm run gen:modules</code> when you add new module files.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>
	</div>
}
